{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "system-prompt-build",
  "title": "How the shared system prompt is built",
  "description": "How agent-config builds `instructions/AGENTS.md`, the one global instruction file every coding agent reads.\n\n**Layout.** There are two rows. On top: Sources (left), Build (middle) and Agent files (right). Below: Prompt blocks (under Sources) and the Apply step (under Build). The six section-file wires run as one line over the top into *Build: wrap and join*. The block-file wires run as one line up the gap between Prompt blocks and Apply into the mcp-protocols generator. The links from the seven agent files run back along the gap between Build and Agent files to AGENTS.md.\n\n- **Sources**: six section files. sections.toml sets order and groups. Principle files, harnesses.toml and task-routing.toml feed the principles and routing generators.\n- **Prompt blocks**: four core MCP servers' `cli.ts instructions` print blocks to mcp_protocols.py, which uses the machines list from mcp/servers.toml. `--write` writes block + sha256 to four block files, and those join in server-name order into the mcp-protocols generator. The red ends are a missing cli.ts and a drift found by --check.\n- **Build**: three generators feed the build step, which writes AGENTS.md. The size limits lead to *Build fails*.\n- **Apply step**: instructions/apply.py runs the build, backs up the stale copy, reads agents.toml, runs mcp_protocols.py --check, exits 1 while stale and creates or repairs the links. Root apply.py runs it after the MCP step. The Hub page edits section files, and every save rebuilds.\n- **Loop**: the orange \"edit through the link\" wire runs from Claude Code's link back to AGENTS.md. The loop note under the agent files explains the backup-and-overwrite and the stale-source cycle.\n\nColors: blue source, violet script or the runs it triggers, green generated, teal symlink, orange edits/Hub, red failure.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
